{"person_id":"jed-mccaleb","name":"Jed McCaleb","cohort_group":"Founders / operators","category":"Cryptocurrency and P2P software founder","birth_year":1975,"age_at_milestone":25,"milestone_by_age_26":"Founded MetaMachine and released eDonkey2000 on September 6, 2000 at age 25, creating one of the world's most popular peer-to-peer file-sharing networks which grew to over 3-4 million concurrent users at its peak.","early_history_summary":"McCaleb was born in Fayetteville, Arkansas and began programming in the 3rd or 4th grade. He attended UC Berkeley but dropped out as a freshman and moved to New York City to work as a programmer. In 2000, at age 25, he founded MetaMachine and released eDonkey2000, a decentralized P2P file-sharing application that became the most popular file-sharing service in the world by the mid-2000s.","primary_leverage_engine":"Technical depth in P2P systems","normalized_primary_engine":"Scarce technical / intellectual depth","secondary_engine":"Structural wave (P2P file-sharing era)","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":2,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":0,"complementary_team_score":1,"structural_wave_score":2,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":1,"total_leverage_score":10,"success_tier":3,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Born in Fayetteville, Arkansas; family relocated to Little Rock where he spent most of his childhood. No specific information about parents' professions or financial status is documented in reviewed sources.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":1,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":1,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":0,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":1,"early_online_platform_community_score":1,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":1,"inherited_access_stack_count":6,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":0,"all_documented_early_condition_count":6,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Self-created domain repetition","primary_early_advantage_tags":"early programming, self-taught, P2P wave, Berkeley dropout, NYC","evidence_summary":"McCaleb began programming in elementary school and was largely self-taught, dropping out of UC Berkeley to pursue hands-on software development in New York City. He built eDonkey2000 at age 25, leveraging deep knowledge of peer-to-peer networking during the Napster-era file-sharing wave. Sam Yagan joined as CEO in 2001, providing a complementary business partnership. No family financial or domain advantages are documented; his early advantage was primarily self-created through years of programming practice and immersion in the P2P technology community.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jed_McCaleb","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jed_McCaleb","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EDonkey2000","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2005-10-23/a-hard-ride-for-edonkey","https://www.forbes.com/profile/jed-mccaleb/"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.3.0-trajectory-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible","starting_point":"Born in Fayetteville, Arkansas to a family that relocated to Little Rock; no parental profession or financial status documented in reviewed sources.","current_position":"Founder and chairman of Vast Space, a private space station company; Forbes net worth approximately $2.9-3.9 billion as of 2025; resides in Berkeley, California.","current_position_year":2025,"is_living":true,"trajectory":[{"year":2000,"age":25,"event":"Founded MetaMachine and released eDonkey2000, a peer-to-peer file-sharing application that became one of the most popular P2P networks globally."},{"year":2006,"age":31,"event":"eDonkey shut down after MetaMachine reached a $30 million settlement with the RIAA over copyright infringement."},{"year":2010,"age":35,"event":"Created Mt. Gox, the first major Bitcoin exchange, repurposing a domain originally intended for Magic: The Gathering card trading."},{"year":2012,"age":37,"event":"Co-founded Ripple (then OpenCoin) with Chris Larsen and Arthur Britto, serving as CTO and helping architect the XRP Ledger."},{"year":2014,"age":39,"event":"Co-founded Stellar, a decentralized payment network designed for fast cross-border transactions, competing with Ripple."},{"year":2021,"age":46,"event":"Founded Vast Space, a private aerospace company aiming to build the world's first commercial space station, self-funding the venture with his crypto fortune."},{"year":2025,"age":50,"event":"Vast Space preparing to launch Haven-1 commercial space station; Forbes estimated net worth of approximately $3.9 billion."}]}
